silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_02_preservation_laws_as_transport_correctness_sections_03_non_functor_counterexample_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In 'NonFunctorCounterexampleYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, the script-introduced shortcut arrow. the transport functor F preserves this typed leg in the Mittens vet-clinic migration; the household-side arrow is named and the clinic-side image is named, with arrow direction and typing kept intact.; also, the functor F sends Mittens to F(Mittens), giving the central object of the transport diagram its clinic-side image." .
